control: A goroutine started through Go is the process's, its panic the failure of what started it, waited for before the slots close, and refused once the process waits
removes: the process closes its slots without waiting for the goroutines Go started
packages: ./process
tests: TestAGoroutineStartedThroughGoIsTheProcesss
scheduled-count: no

diff --git a/process/process.go b/process/process.go
--- a/process/process.go
+++ b/process/process.go
@@ -182,7 +182,6 @@ func (p *proc) joinGoroutines() error {
 	p.goMu.Lock()
